-- Phase 9.4.1 rollback: deliberately NON-destructive.
-- Code from before 9.4.1 (b3399d3) ignores the schedule_* tables, so a rollback is simply deploying the older
-- code: the timetable stays in the database untouched and comes back when 9.4.1+ is deployed again.
-- (VioletDatabase also turns PRAGMA foreign_keys on since 9.4.1; no table before 9.4.1 declares a foreign key, so
-- older code behaves the same with or without it.)
--
-- To really REMOVE the tables, do not edit this file -- use the guarded tool, which refuses while the tables
-- hold any row unless --confirm is given, and then writes a JSON backup of every row before dropping:
--   python -m tools.schedule_rollback --db <path to the database copy> [--confirm] [--backup-dir <folder>]
-- Back up the database file first in any case.
SELECT 'phase94_down: nothing dropped (see the comments above)';
